# Content and Data

## Content Source (Directus)

- All editable user-facing text comes from Directus (see `directus-cms.mdc`).
- CMS content for this site lives under the **Fire Drone** (`firedron`) folder in Directus.
- Do not add marketing copy, labels, or long-form text to components or `data/` when it belongs in CMS.

## Page → Collection Mapping

| App page (`ContentPage`) | Directus singleton | Repeatable collections |
|--------------------------|-------------------|------------------------|
| `global` | `fd_page_global` | `fd_nav_item` |
| `home` | `fd_page_home` | `fd_home_autonomous_hotspot`, `fd_home_carousel_slide`, `fd_home_exploded_annotation` |
| `about-us` | `fd_page_about` | `fd_about_text_block`, `fd_about_list_item` |
| `invest` | `fd_page_invest` | `fd_invest_document` |

Fetch logic and field mapping: `lib/directus/content.ts`. Schema and field definitions: `scripts/directus-page-schema.mjs`.

## Data-First Structure (Non-CMS)

- Use `data/` only for non-CMS configuration: layout constants, static asset paths, UI defaults.
- Use `data/*.ts` for plain objects/arrays that are not CMS-managed.
- Use `data/*.tsx` only when content truly needs JSX fragments and is not stored in Directus.
- Avoid embedding long repeated text directly in page components.

## Typing Patterns

- Infer mapped-item types from source data where practical.
- Preferred style: `(typeof projects)[number]`.
- Page section shapes: `types/content.ts` (`PageSections`, `SectionContentMap`).

## Content Consistency

- Preserve Czech-first tone and terminology unless task states otherwise.
- Keep wording consistent across navigation, cards, hero text, and FAQ.
- For regulatory/investment wording, prioritize clarity and trust over hype.

## Link and Asset Content Rules

- Keep downloadable files and static assets in `public/`.
- Ensure all external links use safe attributes when opening new tabs.
- Keep image alt text descriptive and localized to page language.
